# Build-context exclusions for the release image built by ./Dockerfile.
#
# The builder stage copies this context into /monero (`COPY . .`) and then
# configures CMake at /monero/build, so anything a developer built in this
# checkout has to stay out of the context. A host `build/` tree carries a
# CMakeCache.txt full of absolute host paths, and CMake aborts as soon as it is
# copied in:
#
#   CMake Error: The current CMakeCache.txt directory /monero/build/CMakeCache.txt
#   is different than the directory <host-checkout>/build where CMakeCache.txt was
#   created. ... The source "/monero/CMakeLists.txt" does not match the source
#   "<host-checkout>/CMakeLists.txt" used to generate cache.
#
# Without this file `docker build .` therefore succeeds on a fresh clone -- which
# is why CI, which always builds a fresh checkout, never saw it -- and fails in
# every checkout that has been built locally.
#
# `.git` is deliberately NOT excluded. cmake/GitVersion.cmake reads the working
# tree to stamp the daemon's version string (`v0.18.1.0-<commit>`); with no Git
# data it falls back to version.cmake, whose `export-subst` placeholders are
# substituted only by `git archive`, and the released binary then reports
# `-unknown`. The builder stage is discarded by the multi-stage build -- the
# published image holds only /monerod and the empty /data directory -- so Git
# history in the context reaches no artefact.

# CMake build trees: the in-tree `build/` the top-level Makefile and README use,
# the out-of-tree `build-*` trees the toolchain matrix uses, and the artefacts an
# in-source configure leaves behind.
/build
/build-*
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/CMakeFiles
**/cmake_install.cmake
**/compile_commands.json

# contrib/depends outputs. The builder runs `make -C contrib/depends` itself; a
# prefix, work tree or source cache built for a different host must not be
# mistaken for its own.
/contrib/depends/built
/contrib/depends/work
/contrib/depends/sources
/contrib/depends/*-*-*

# Daemon and wallet logs or runtime state left behind by a local run.
**/*.log
/testnet
/stagenet

# Editor, tooling and automation scratch directories. None is a build input.
/blitzy
/.vscode
/.idea
/.cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
